  "_about": "a great hornbill in flight: the big black-and-white bird of the forest canopy -- the huge, gently down-curved bill, blunt at its tip, yellow with an orange-red base, and over it the great flat-topped casque, broad, flat-topped and U-shaped from the front, yellow, black where it meets the forehead; the head and face black, the neck and shoulders creamy yellow-white; black wings crossed by a broad pale bar and edged white behind; the long white tail with a broad black band across it; white thighs and vent, a red eye; grey feet that close round a bough (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
